I got tetris-v compiled without a lot of trouble. When I run it, though,
as soon as a line is full, it complains about a bad call to _showstring
and dumps core. The complaint occurs at either the call to refresh() in
scbeep, or the call to refresh() in main_loop, depending on whether the
-s switch is used at execution time. I tried attacking it with sdb, but
it proved to be impenetrable to me.

Environment is Microport System V/AT 2.4 (with the 2.4 curses library),
and compiled in the small model. 
